"Benjamin Strober", "first_name": "Benjamin", "last_name": "Strober", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 271965, "full_name": "Selene K. Swanson", "first_name": "Selene K.", "last_name": "Swanson", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 66526, "full_name": "Laurence Florens", "first_name": "Laurence", "last_name": "Florens", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Laurence_Florens", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 513974, "full_name": "James E. Bradner", "first_name": "James E.", "last_name": "Bradner", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 2473, "full_name": "Myles Brown", "first_name": "Myles", "last_name": "Brown", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Myles_Brown", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1351938, "full_name": "Peter M. Howley", "first_name": "Peter M.", "last_name": "Howley", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 127447, "full_name": "Megha Padi", "first_name": "Megha", "last_name": "Padi", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 127462, "full_name": "Michael P. Washburn", "first_name": "Michael P.", "last_name": "Washburn", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 127469, "full_name": "James A. DeCaprio", "first_name": "James", "last_name": "A. DeCaprio", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/ST_requires_MYCL_to_sustain_MCC_viability_/5499847", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>(A) CRISPR-Cas9 screen of MKL-1 cells was analyzed in the MAGeCK-VISPR pipeline. Cumulative distribution function of p-values plotted based on 18,493 human genes. EP400 complex components and MYCL were identified in CRISPR screen negative selection with p-values < 0.05 were indicated. See also <a href=\"http://www.plospathogens.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.ppat.1006668#ppat.1006668.s003\" target=\"_blank\">S3A\u2013S3C Fig</a> and <a href=\"http://www.plospathogens.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.ppat.1006668#ppat.1006668.s011\" target=\"_blank\">S2 Table</a>. (B) Lysates from virus-positive MCC cell lines MKL-1, WaGa, MS-1, PeTa, BroLi and MKL-2, virus-negative MCC cell line UISO, and additional lines were immunoblotted. ST-CT are UISO cells stably expressing C-terminal epitope tagged ST. (C) Lysates from MKL-1 cell lines containing Dox-inducible shRNA (shMYCL) or miRNA (mirMYCL) specific for MYCL, prepared 2 days after addition of 0.3 \u03bcg/ml Dox (Input), were immunoprecipitated for MAX, Ab5, EP400 or non-specific IgG and blotted. (D) MKL-1 cells containing Dox-inducible HA tagged Omomyc before (-) or after (+) 5 days of Dox treatment. Dox (0.3 \u03bcg/ml) was added every two days. Lysates (Input) were immunoprecipitated with non-specific IgG, MAX, Ab5 and HA antibodies and blotted. (E) Viability of MKL-1 Dox-inducible cell lines described in C and D. 3,000 cells of each line were aliquoted in 96 well plate on day 0. Total days of Dox treatment is indicated on the X axis. Fresh medium or medium with 0.3 \u03bcg/ml Dox was supplemented every two days. At the end of time course (day 10), all samples were assessed for viability by CellTiter-Glo (Promega). Values were normalized to untreated samples of each inducible cell line. Three biological replicas were performed. Data are presented as mean (SD).</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 991176, "created_date": "2017-10-13T17:37:55Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-12T11:04:12Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["PP 2A subunits", "protein phosphatase 2", "RB", "genome-wide CRISPR-Cas 9 screen", "MCC cell lines", "L-MYC", "gene expression", "tumor suppressor function", "15- component EP 400 histone acetyltransferase", "MYC h